  "id": "Compound::DB01610 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Valganciclovir is shown to bind to Slc15a2, a protein that participates in multiple transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide secondary active transmembrane transport, peptide/proton symport, and oligopeptide transport. These activities are all associated with the transport of peptides across cellular membranes, a process that is critical for nutrient uptake and cellular homeostasis. The evidence suggests that Valganciclovir may influence Slc15a1 through its interaction with Slc15a2, potentially modulating the transport of peptides by targeting the transporter activity of Slc15a2. The shared involvement of Slc15a2 in multiple transport mechanisms implies a functional overlap between the two entities, and the binding of Valganciclovir to Slc15a2 may serve as a regulatory mechanism that affects the activity of Slc15a1. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc15a2 as a central mediator in the transport process, and the relationship between Valganciclovir and Slc15a1 is likely mediated through this protein.",
